EXT. SCHOOL BUS GRAVEYARD - DUSK

Forty yellow buses rust nose to tail in a field of dead sunflowers. Windows gone. Seats full of weeds.

PRAKASH "PAKS" NAIR, 16, lanky, glasses, stands on a bus roof with a stolen six-pack.

WYATT BOONE, 17, buzzcut, football jacket, climbs up after him. He grins too hard.

Below, LUCIA ORTEGA, 16, braids, sketchbook under her arm, watches them both.

WYATT
Thought you'd chicken out.

PAKS
So did I.

Wyatt snatches a can. Paks grabs it back. They shove. The roof BOOMS under their boots.

Both freeze.

A siren, far off. Coming closer.

LUCIA
Cops!

Wyatt and Paks scramble, tumble down the rear emergency door. Lucia is already running. Cans spill in the dust.

They hit the sunflowers, all three, laughing like idiots.
